# No bloat content

When creating pages, components, stories, or copy: ship only what the product needs. Do not pad UI with demo, meta, or borrowed branding.

## Product identity

- This app is **Citizen Wing Commander** (JustWorks Digital). It is **not** Spectrum, RSI.com, or any CIG tool.
- Visual theme may be RSI/Spectrum-*inspired* (see `rsi-theme.mdc`). That does **not** mean naming or mimicking their products in UI copy, nav, CTAs, or status chrome.
- Do **not** put labels like “Spectrum”, “Roberts Space Industries”, “CIG”, or faux org channels on product surfaces unless the user explicitly asks for that reference.

## No scaffold filler

- Avoid placeholder “systems check”, token lectures, Storybook launch ads, design-system marketing, or meta notes about Tailwind/`bg-rsi-*` on user-facing pages.
- New elements: real domain content (sessions, missions, checklists, players) or a minimal empty state — not decorative industrial flavor text.
- Storybook / foundation docs can document tokens and theme; the app shell should not.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — looks like Spectrum / design-system demo
<button>Spectrum</button>
<p>Companion systems online</p>
<p>Use bg-rsi-* and CSS variables — avoid one-off hex</p>

// ✅ GOOD — product-owned, purpose-built
<h1>Citizen Wing Commander</h1>
<p>Plan hauling sessions with your crew.</p>
```
